// expect-error: NITPICK-TYPE-099
// expect-error-at: 32:1
//
// PROBE 19b -- A CLAIM OF `Copy` FOR A TYPE THE CLAIMING TREE DOES NOT
// DECLARE IS REFUSED BEFORE THE JUDGEMENT IS ASKED (cycle 0.4.0a, TM-265).
//
// ASKS: may code in this tree declare `string` -- a builtin -- `Copy`, the
// prelude's trait? It is `probe19`'s question as it stood until cycle 0.4.0a,
// and its text.
//
// MATTERS BECAUSE `vec_at<T: Copy>` hands an element back by value
// (`SAFETY.md` S-18h, TM-211), and the bound is worth something only if the
// language decides who may claim it: a claim of `Copy` for an owning type
// would make `vec_at` hand back a second owner of the element.
//
// ANSWER, measured at compiler `2e1cb4a`: NO, by a rule asked first. An impl
// names a type or a trait declared in its own manifest's tree, or it is
// `NITPICK-TYPE-099` at the impl (the compiler's D-359, landing 124), asked
// before coherence and the `Copy` judgement: `string` is a builtin and `Copy`
// the prelude's, so this impl names neither -- "an impl names at least one
// type or trait declared in its own manifest's tree (D-359)" -- once. A
// consumer's `impl:Bytes:Copy`, in a tree of its own, is refused the same
// way, measured: a consumer can claim `Copy` for no type it does not declare,
// and a type's own tree is refused by the judgement when the type owns
// (`probe19`). THE REFUSAL IS THE ASSERTION (B-7). ITS CONTROL is this file
// at compiler `7e91730`, before the orphan rule, where the judgement answered,
// `NITPICK-TYPE-087`, once, at the impl.
mod:probe19b_orphan_copy_refused;

use "../../src/core/vec.npk".*;

impl:string:Copy = { };

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
    exit 0i32;
};

// A SUPERSET of what `NITPICK-REACH-002` asks, deliberately (`SAFETY.md` S-6b,
// constraint 3: a superset compiles). If a later compiler reordered its phases
// so that the reach analysis ran before the check this file asserts, a
// failsafe naming exactly the demanded arms could add a stray `REACH-002` to
// the refusal; this one cannot.
func:failsafe = int32(Error:e) {
    pick (e) {
        (HeapBadRequest)    { exit 91i32; },
        (HeapOom)           { exit 92i32; },
        (IntOverflow)       { exit 93i32; },
        (OutOfBounds)       { exit 94i32; },
        (Unreachable)       { exit 95i32; },
        (WildLeak)          { exit 96i32; },
        (DivByZero)         { exit 97i32; },
        (DivOverflow)       { exit 98i32; },
        (StackExhausted)    { exit 106i32; },
        (MachineFault)      { exit 107i32; },
        (DecreasesViolated) { exit 108i32; },
        (LimitViolated)     { exit 109i32; },
        (*)                 { exit 99i32; }
    }
    exit 9i32;
};
